			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Hydrate URI results and use Mountain for glob-based extension activation\n\nTwo related improvements to the workspace namespace and extension activation flow:\n\n1. URI Result Hydration: Add `HydrateUriResults` helper that converts string URLs returned from Mountain's `findFiles` effect into proper `vscode.Uri` objects. Extensions expect `result[i].fsPath` / `.scheme` / `.toString()` to work, but Mountain returns raw strings. Uses Stock VS Code's `URI.parse()` to create fully-functional URI instances.\n\n2. Mountain-Backed Glob Activation: Add `FolderContainsGlobViaMountain` that calls `findFiles(glob, {maxResults:1})` via gRPC. The activation logic now:\n   - Uses native stat for literal filenames (package.json, Cargo.toml)\n   - Uses Mountain's parallel `ignore::WalkBuilder` for glob patterns (**/*.csproj, src/**/manifest.yml)\n   - Falls back to local Node walker on Mountain miss/IPC failure\n\nThis speeds up extension activation on large repos by leveraging Mountain's OS-threaded, gitignore-aware walker with early-exit, while preserving the fast-path stat for literal probes.",
			"SHA": "5619ec672aa24ac4a5e333815bae0b940c7af3b7"
